          "path": "client/src/test/java/com/google/cloud/gcs/analyticscore/client/GcsObjectRangeTest.java",
          "line": 28,
          "diff_hunk": "ations under the License.\n+ */\n+\n+package com.google.cloud.gcs.analyticscore.client;\n+\n+import static com.google.common.truth.Truth.assertThat;\n+import static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.assertThrows;\n+\n+import java.nio.ByteBuffer;\n+import java.util.HashSet;\n+import java.util.Set;\n+import java.util.concurrent.CompletableFuture;\n+import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;\n+\n+class GcsObjectRangeTest {",
          "body": "`GcsObjectCombinedRange` is an `@AutoValue` class, and the only hand-written logic on it is `union()` (which already exercises `toBuilder()` and `builder()`). These 8 tests are exercising code generated by the AutoValue processor (`AutoValue_GcsObjectCombinedRange`) and coupling to AutoValue's internal error messages (`\"Missing required properties\"`).\n\nCan we drop the generated-code tests here and keep just the two new `union_*` tests (`union_withPrecedingRange_updatesStartOffsetAndLength` and `union_withEncompassingRange_...`), which genuinely add coverage for the `newOffset < getOffset()` path",
          "created_at": "2026-11-04T10:53:46Z",
          "url": "https://github.com/GoogleCloudPlatform/gcs-analytics-core/pull/468#discussion_r4466592971"
        },
        {
          "id": "pull_comment:4466604115",
          "comment_id": 4466604115,
