          "thread_id": "PRRT_kwDOPmMU8s6zjqW7",
          "type": "inline_review_comment",
          "author": "shrutisinghania",
          "path": "client/src/test/java/com/google/cloud/gcs/analyticscore/client/GcsCombinedObjectRangeTest.java",
          "line": 84,
          "diff_hunk": "@@ -78,6 +81,181 @@ void union_withContainedRange_returnsContainingRange() {\n     assertThat(result.getLength()).isEqualTo(200); // (100 + 200) - 100\n   }\n \n+  @Test",
          "body": "`GcsObjectRange` is a pure `@AutoValue` class with no custom methods, validation, or defaults\u2014every method tested here (`builder`, `set*`, `build`, `equals`, `hashCode`, `toString`) is generated by AutoValue and already exercised transitively by `GcsCombinedObjectRangeTest`, `VectoredIoUtilTest`, and the channel tests.\n\nUnless we're adding custom precondition checks to `GcsObjectRange.Builder`, we shouldn't need a dedicated test suite for AutoValue's codegen. Suggest reducing it to a single build-and-read round-trip test if we want a basic smoke check",
